      "destructive_hint": true,
      "idempotent_hint": true,
      "open_world_hint": true,
      "read_only_hint": false,
      "title": "Delete a flow"
    },
    "description": "Delete one of your saved flows. Deleting one that is not there is not an error.\n\nA flow in the shared 'global' library cannot be deleted here, and a caller that named no session has no library of its own to delete from.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "name"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "delete_flow"
  },
  "dialog": {
    "annotations": {
      "destructive_hint": true,
      "idempotent_hint": false,
      "open_world_hint": true,
      "read_only_hint": false,
      "title": "Answer a native dialog"
    },
    "description": "Answer a native alert, confirm or prompt: accept, dismiss, read (see the message without answering), or send_text (fill a prompt with text and accept it).\n\nAn open dialog blocks every other command, so if a call fails on an unexpected alert, clear it here.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "default": "accept",
          "enum": [
            "accept",
            "dismiss",
            "read",
            "send_text"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "text": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "wait_timeout": {
          "default": 10,
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "dialog"
  },
  "drag": {
    "annotations": {
      "destructive_hint": true,
      "idempotent_hint": false,
      "open_world_hint": true,
      "read_only_hint": false,
      "title": "Drag an element"
    },
    "description": "Drag an element onto another element (to), or by an offset in pixels (by_x, by_y); give one or the other. A range slider is by_x; a card into a column is to.\n\nThe pointer presses, glides and releases with short holds at each end, which drag libraries need. On Chrome this also completes native HTML5 drag-and-drop; on Firefox it does not, so a draggable=true element there may need the page's own fallback.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "by_x": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "by_y": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "glide": {
          "default": true,
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "selector": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "description": "Which element: {\"css\": \"button.go\"} or {\"xpath\": \"//button[@type='submit']\"} - exactly one of the two.",
              "properties": {
                "css": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ],
                  "default": null,
                  "description": "A CSS selector, e.g. button[type=submit]"
                },
                "xpath": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ],
                  "default": null,
                  "description": "An XPath expression, e.g. //button[@type='submit']"
                }
              },
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "to": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "description": "Which element: {\"css\": \"button.go\"} or {\"xpath\": \"//button[@type='submit']\"} - exactly one of the two.",
              "properties": {
                "css": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ],
                  "default": null,
                  "description": "A CSS selector, e.g. button[type=submit]"
                },
                "xpath": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ],
                  "default": null,
                  "description": "An XPath expression, e.g. //button[@type='submit']"
                }
              },
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "url": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "wait_timeout": {
          "default": 30,
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "drag"
  },
  "end_browser": {
    "annotations": {
      "destructive_hint": true,
      "idempotent_hint": true,
      "open_world_hint": true,
      "read_only_hint": false,
      "title": "End browser"
    },
    "description": "Quit this session's browser and free its Grid slot.\n\nCall it when finished, and on failure paths too: browsers are scarce, and an\nabandoned one holds its slot until the Grid reaps it. The session survives,\nso a later open_session() comes back to the same page. Files the browser had\nand you did not keep go with it.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "end_browser"
  },
  "execute_script": {
    "annotations": {
      "destructive_hint": true,
      "idempotent_hint": false,
      "open_world_hint": true,
      "read_only_hint": false,
      "title": "Run JavaScript in the page"
    },
    "description": "Run JavaScript in the page and return what it returns.\n\nCheck the other tools first: interact, write, extract and outline cover most\nneeds, and only interact's hover opens a menu that appears on :hover, which\nscript events never trigger. Use this for what is left: scrolling\n(window.scrollTo), computed styles, reading many values at once, direct DOM\nwork. Not for drag and drop; drag uses real pointer input.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "script": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "url": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "script"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "execute_script"
  },
