    },
    "description": "A mouse action on an element: click, double_click, right_click, hover or scroll_to.\n\nhover leaves the pointer where it put it, so a menu that opens on hover stays open for the next call: hover it, then click inside. scroll_to brings an off-screen element into view.\n\nThe pointer jumps onto the element unless glide=true, which moves it in small steps, for interfaces that react to movement: sliders, sortable lists, menus that track direction. To drag something, use drag.\n\nReturns the URL and title after the action, so a navigation it caused shows.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "enum": [
            "click",
            "double_click",
            "right_click",
            "hover",
